SUMMARY:Sunday Sounds | Sean Gaskell
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an afternoon of music and art in the Museum. With a soundscape of the West African kora harp\, we invite you to experience artwork in the galleries in a more emotional and sensory way. \nABOUT THE MUSICIAN\nSean Gaskell features songs on the kora- a 21 stringed West African harp. He studied under the extensive instruction of Moriba Kuyateh and the late Malamini Jobarteh in Gambia\, and both Youssoupha Cissokho and Mamadou Cissokho in Senegal. The kora is traditionally played by oral historians known as Griots. Many songs featured on the kora preserve an 800-year history dating back to the founding of the Mande empire. Gaskell has presented adult\, youth and family programs at over 500 libraries and a multitude of k-12 schools\, colleges\, universities and assisted living facilities throughout the United States and Canada. \nFor more information\, please visit www.seangaskell.com \nRESERVE TICKETS NOW
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/sunday-sounds-sean-gaskell/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Wellness
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/3n6a3241_optimized-scaled.jpg
